libdcerpc is considered EXPERIMENTAL at this point.
The API is unstable and subject to change.

libdcerpc is a DCE/RPC library. It uses libsmb2 named pipes as
transport and implements NDR32/NDR64 as well as YAML and JSON coders for
the srvsvc, lsarpc, samr, dssetup, netlogon, winreg, wkssvc and epm
interfaces.

libdcerpc is distributed under the 2-Clause BSD licence. See COPYING.

  Link with:  -ldcerpc -lsmb2
  pkg-config: libdcerpc

Public headers are installed under <dcerpc/>.

Platforms
=========
libdcerpc is Linux only for now. It can not be built on Windows since its
symbols collide with Microsoft's own RPC libraries.

Releases
========
libdcerpc lives in the libsmb2 git repository, in the libdcerpc/
directory, but has its own version, soname and releases. Releases are
tagged libdcerpc-<version>. A release tarball contains only this
directory and builds against an installed libsmb2 (>= 7.0.0).

Building
========
Standalone, against an installed libsmb2 found with pkg-config:

  autoreconf -fi
  ./configure [--enable-examples]
  make
  make install

or with CMake:

  cmake [-DENABLE_EXAMPLES=ON] [-DENABLE_UTILS=OFF] <srcdir>
  make
  make install

Without libsmb2
---------------
libdcerpc can also be built without any dependency on libsmb2:

  ./configure --without-libsmb2
or
  cmake -DWITH_LIBSMB2=OFF <srcdir>

This builds only the coders and the server runtime. Use it in a server
that has its own SMB2 transport: <dcerpc/server.h> takes the bytes
clients write to a named pipe, does BIND and fragmentation, dispatches
the requests to stub implementations through the coders and gives back
the bytes to return to their reads. The coders can also be used directly,
with a context from dcerpc_create_context(NULL). Binding and calls, the
client side, are not available and fail with -EINVAL. The utilities and
the examples are not built.

From the libsmb2 tree, libdcerpc is built together with libsmb2 against
the uninstalled library (disable with ./configure --disable-libdcerpc or
cmake -DENABLE_LIBDCERPC=OFF).

RPMs are built with packaging/RPM/makerpms.sh. It needs a libdcerpc-*
tag and libsmb2-devel installed.

Utilities
=========
dcerpc      : send DCE/RPC requests described as YAML or JSON
              (see dcerpc-examples/)
epm-enum    : list the endpoints registered with the endpoint mapper
winreg-tui  : browse a remote registry (needs ncurses)
